---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why this exists - Awesome GitHub"
  description="Why the Awesome GitHub site exists and how the phased delivery plan works."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Context</div>
    <h1>Why this exists</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The site gives LightSpeed a clean public face for the ideas already living inside
      the `.github` repository: governance, reusable patterns, and the discipline that
      keeps AI-assisted workflows maintainable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <p>
        The first release is intentionally small. It proves the site structure, the voice,
        and the navigation without waiting for the full content library.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Shows the repository as a control plane rather than a document dump.</li>
        <li>Keeps the launchable scope to three pages.</li>
        <li>Creates a clean foundation for the fuller resource catalogue in phase 2.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How phase 2 grows</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <p>
        Once phase 1 is live, the site can add richer browsing, category pages, resource
        previews, and search. The goal is to reuse the same design language rather than
        reset it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
